### Step 1 — `build` → `BuildOwner.java`
```java
public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built)
        throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
    require("firstName", request.getFirstName(), missing);
    require("lastName", request.getLastName(), missing);
    require("address", request.getAddress(), missing);
    require("city", request.getCity(), missing);
    require("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);
    if (!missing.isEmpty()) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
    }
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(request);
    LocalDate effective = owner.getRegistrationDate() == null ? LocalDate.now() : owner.getRegistrationDate();
    owner.setRegistrationDate(BusinessDay.nextBusinessDay(effective));
    built.set(owner);
}

private static void require(String field, String value, List<String> missing) {
    if (value == null || value.isBlank()) {
        missing.add(field);
    }
}
```
Side-effects: manual required-field check (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone) → throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400) listing blanks; maps DTO→`Owner`; sets `registrationDate` to the supplied date (or today), rolled forward to the next business day via `BusinessDay`; publishes `Out<Owner>`. This is the only step that reads the body.

`BusinessDay.nextBusinessDay`: Saturday → +2 days, Sunday → +1 day, weekdays unchanged.

### Step 2 — `validatePostcode` → `ValidateOwnerPostcode.java`
```java
private static final Map<String, int[]> REGION_RANGE = Map.of(
        "NSW", new int[] {2000, 2099}, "VIC", new int[] {3000, 3099}, "QLD", new int[] {4000, 4099});

public void service(@Val Owner owner) throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
    if (postcode == null) {
        return;
    }
    int[] range = REGION_RANGE.get(Locality.of(owner));
    if (!postcode.matches("[0-9]{4}")
            || (range != null && (Integer.parseInt(postcode) < range[0] || Integer.parseInt(postcode) > range[1]))) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(List.of("postcode"));
    }
}
```
Postcode is optional (null → skip). When present must be 4 digits; if the city maps to a known region (via `Locality`), must fall in NSW 2000-2099 / VIC 3000-3099 / QLD 4000-4099. Invalid → `MissingOwnerFieldsException(["postcode"])` (400).

`Locality.of(owner)`: first tries to derive region from the postcode digits (2000-2099→NSW, 3000-3099→VIC, 4000-4099→QLD); else from a city table (Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD); else `UNKNOWN`.

### Step 3 — `normalizeAddress` → `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java`
```java
private static final Map<String, String> ABBREVIATIONS = Map.of("ST", "STREET", "RD", "ROAD", "AVE", "AVENUE");

public void service(@Val Owner owner) throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    String address = owner.getAddress() == null ? "" : owner.getAddress().trim();
    if (address.isEmpty()) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(List.of("address"));
    }
    StringBuilder normalized = new StringBuilder();
    for (String token : address.split("\\s+")) {
        String upper = token.toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);
        if (normalized.length() > 0) {
            normalized.append(' ');
        }
        normalized.append(ABBREVIATIONS.getOrDefault(upper, upper));
    }
    owner.setAddress(normalized.toString());
}
```
Mutates the `Owner` in place: trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, expands ST→STREET, RD→ROAD, AVE→AVENUE. Blank after trim → 400 (`["address"]`).

### Step 4 — `normalizeTelephone` → `NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    String e164 = E164Telephone.toE164(owner.getTelephone());
    if (e164 == null) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(List.of("telephone"));
    }
    owner.setTelephone(e164);
}
```
Rewrites telephone to E.164 in place; unconvertible → 400 (`["telephone"]`).

`E164Telephone.toE164`: keeps leading `+` and country code if present; otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`; strips non-digits; returns null unless 8-15 digits after `+`, and enforces `+61`→exactly 9 national digits, `+1`→exactly 10.

### Step 5 — `normalizeEmail` → `NormalizeOwnerEmail.java`
```java
private static final Pattern EMAIL = Pattern.compile("^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$");

public void service(@Val Owner owner) throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    String email = owner.getEmail();
    if (email == null || email.isBlank()) {
        return;
    }
    if (!EMAIL.matcher(email).matches()) {
        throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(List.of("email"));
    }
    owner.setEmail(email.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT));
}
```
Email optional (null/blank → skip). If present must match the regex, else 400 (`["email"]`); valid value is lower-cased in place.

### Step 6 — `rejectDuplicateIdentity` → `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity.java`
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateOwnerIdentityException {
    String telephone = IdentityKey.telephone(owner);
    String email = IdentityKey.email(owner);
    for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (other != owner && telephone.equals(IdentityKey.telephone(other))
                && email.equals(IdentityKey.email(other))) {
            throw new DuplicateOwnerIdentityException(IdentityKey.of(owner));
        }
    }
}
```
Scans all owners; if another owner has the same normalized E.164 telephone AND same lower-cased email, throws `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409). `IdentityKey.of` = `telephone + '|' + email + '|' + HouseholdId.of(owner)` (household id is a SHA-256-derived 16-hex-char digest of normalized lastName+address), but the collision check itself only compares telephone+email.

### Step 7 — `rejectCityAtCapacity` → `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity.java`
```java
private static final int CAPACITY = 50;

public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) throws CityAtCapacityException {
    String city = normalize(owner.getCity());
    int count = 0;
    for (Owner other : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (other != owner && city.equals(normalize(other.getCity())) && ++count >= CAPACITY) {
            throw new CityAtCapacityException(owner.getCity());
        }
    }
}

private static String normalize(String value) {
    return value == null ? "" : value.trim().toLowerCase();
}
```
If the city already holds ≥50 owners (case-insensitive, trimmed), throws `CityAtCapacityException` (409). New owner not yet saved, so the 51st into a city of 50 is rejected.

